        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe `'cmdline'` completion is unfortunately [known to have issues](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/7c2caf0ae915d819f2f39467d6bb9313c2b3e90a/doc/mini-input.txt#L848-L853) when it comes to computing the completion base. Right now it works as expected if there is a `fuzzy` flag in 'wildoptions' since it will use `matchfuzzy`. For example, adding `vim.o.wildoptions = 'pum,fuzzy'` line to the 'init.lua' fixes the issue.\n\nI'll take a look if this can be improved, but in any case 'mini.input' is not meant to serve as a 100% replacement for the command line.",
